            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "How to center only header? Rest of content should centered but left-aligned (as it is currently). I have `header = \"NVIM \" .. tostring(vim.version())` and would like to add to the default content some other stats like number of packages loaded, startup time, etc. if possible (especially with native Neovim functions).\r\n\r\nThanks in advance! I will probably not use this start screen on vim launch (I tend to launch one as a scratchpad often) and instead use a mapping to show the screen on demand. ",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">How to center only header? Rest of content should centered but left-aligned (as it is currently). I have <code class=\"notranslate\">header = \"NVIM \" .. tostring(vim.version())</code> and would like to add to the default content some other stats like number of packages loaded, startup time, etc. if possible (especially with native Neovim functions).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks in advance! I will probably not use this start screen on vim launch (I tend to launch one as a scratchpad often) and instead use a mapping to show the screen on demand.</p>",
