                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> How to center only header? Rest of content should centered but left-aligned (as it is currently). I have `header = \"NVIM \" .. tostring(vim.version())` and would like to add to the default content some other stats like number of packages loaded, startup time, etc. if possible (especially with native Neovim functions).\r\n\r\nThere is no easy way to do this at the moment unfortunately. The general direction is to write custom content hooks in `config.content_hooks`. There are [couple of example](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-starter.html#ministarter-example-config) and [`refresh()` docs](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-starter.html#ministarter.refresh) can give more details as to how content is computed.\r\n\r\nI do agree that it is a bit hard to customize 'mini.starter' appearance, but that was an intentional design decision to make it noticeably easier to customize its items.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFor the future: a separate new question deserves a separate discussion. This way its reply will not be misplaced in an unrelated thread which is more useful for the future users to search.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How to center only header? Rest of content should centered but left-aligned (as it is currently). I have <code class=\"notranslate\">header = \"NVIM \" .. tostring(vim.version())</code> and would like to add to the default content some other stats like number of packages loaded, startup time, etc. if possible (especially with native Neovim functions).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is no easy way to do this at the moment unfortunately. The general direction is to write custom content hooks in <code class=\"notranslate\">config.content_hooks</code>. There are <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-starter.html#ministarter-example-config\" rel=\"nofollow\">couple of example</a> and <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-starter.html#ministarter.refresh\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">refresh()</code> docs</a> can give more details as to how content is computed.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I do agree that it is a bit hard to customize 'mini.starter' appearance, but that was an intentional design decision to make it noticeably easier to customize its items.</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For the future: a separate new question deserves a separate discussion. This way its reply will not be misplaced in an unrelated thread which is more useful for the future users to search.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "How to center only header? Rest of content should centered but left-aligned (as it is currently). I have header = \"NVIM \" .. tostring(vim.version()) and would like to add to the default content some other stats like number of packages loaded, startup time, etc. if possible (especially with native Neovim functions).\n\nThere is no easy way to do this at the moment unfortunately. The general direction is to write custom content hooks in config.content_hooks. There are couple of example and refresh() docs can give more details as to how content is computed.\nI do agree that it is a bit hard to customize 'mini.starter' appearance, but that was an intentional design decision to make it noticeably easier to customize its items.\n\nFor the future: a separate new question deserves a separate discussion. This way its reply will not be misplaced in an unrelated thread which is more useful for the future users to search.",
